# Build output
/mailroom
/dist/
*.exe
# `go build` inside the notices generator's own module leaves its binary beside the source.
# `make notices` uses `go run` and produces nothing, but the mistake is an easy one to make.
/scripts/notices/notices

# Local state — never commit; contains sealed credentials and grant history
/data/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
client_secret*.json
credentials*.json
# A captured Google console session is a live login, not a config file.
*console-session*.json

# Local working notes, not for the public history
/tasks/
/scratch/
NOTES.local.md

# Editor and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Go
/vendor/
*.test
coverage.out

# Terraform working directories. Provider binaries run to hundreds of megabytes, and state
# files hold resource detail that does not belong in a public repository. The dependency lock
# file is deliberately not in this list: it pins provider versions and checksums, so committing
# it is what makes a stranger's `terraform init` resolve the same providers this repository was
# tested against.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log

# Downloaded build tools. The Tailwind standalone binary is over a hundred megabytes and
# `make css` fetches it on demand; nothing here belongs in the history.
/.tools/

# The UI review set's generated half. `make ui-shots` rebuilds pages/ and narrow/ from the
# templates in one command, so committing 160 PNGs bought a bigger clone and nothing else.
# The contact sheets, before/ and fixes/ stay tracked: no command can put those back.
/docs/ui/screenshots/pages/
/docs/ui/screenshots/narrow/
